To 3D print the components for the gearbox, follow this guide. 

Step 1 'uploading the hardware': Open the program PrusaSlicer. To import a component of the Gearbox into the PrusaSlicer program, first download the file of the desired component. The components can be found in the map 'Hardware'. 
Then, upload it to the prusasliser by clicking on the most left box icon on the top bar. See picture 1. It asks you to select a file that you want to add.
Select the desired component and upload it in medium quality. See picture 2. It will give a schematic overview of the component on the horizontal plane. The largest part should go on top. 
This can be done by clicking on the desired component. On the left side of the screen there are different options. Select the fourth option from above called 'place to face'. See picture 3. 
Now you can click on the side of the component that you want to face down. 

Repeat this for all the components and allign them on the board.

Step 2 'setting up the printer settings':
In the top right of the screen, you see 'printer settings:', 'Filament' and 'printer'.
For print settings, choose the '0.20 mm STRUCTURAL', for the filament, choose the 'Prusa PLA - black' and for the printer, choose one of the available printers with nozzle setting 0.4 mm. 


On the right of the screen, there is a vertical slider.
Adjusting it gives you insight in the different layers. Slide both sides up and down. In case you see a dark blue part in the component appearing, it needs support. To give this support,
there are 3 different options on the right of the screen under 'supports'. For the components that we are rpinting, it suffices to select support on build plate only.

